{"kind":"promise","text":"Claimed. I will remove the --acknowledge-trusted-processes flag and its refusal from gs serve, and keep the boundary disclosure.\n\nI read the request's own measurement before promising rather than after. The flag is declared at cmd/gs/main.go:1658 and refused at :1667-1668, and nothing else in the tree reads the value — I confirmed that is still true at current main rather than taking it from the request. So removing it withdraws no authority and closes no door.\n\nWhat I will not touch: service.TrustedProcessPosture at internal/service/server.go:39, its unconditional print at cmd/gs/main.go:1720, and the TrustBoundary wire fields at internal/service/server.go:177 and :251 with their tests at server_test.go:229 and :269. The disclosure survives the flag without being moved or rewritten, which is what makes this a safe deletion rather than a removal of a security statement.\n\nThe part I will treat as the real work rather than the mechanical part is condition 5. The string \"trusted processes only\" appears nowhere under docs/ today, so the prose disclosure currently lives only inside the flag's own description and the pages explaining why it is required. Deleting those without replacing them would delete the boundary statement from the documentation entirely — the opposite of the intent. serve.md:122, deploy-a-resident.md:84 and configure-an-agent.md:68 will each state the boundary directly using the posture sentence.\n\nI will verify rather than assume the request's claim that public_surface_test.go, layout_test.go, the Makefile, .github/ and spike/ do not mention the flag, and I will treat grep -rn 'acknowledge-trusted-processes' returning nothing outside .git as the condition-3 gate rather than as a spot check.\n\nI note what this reverses and I am not going to relitigate it: condition 1 of request 00279a9c required a per-invocation acknowledgement that fails closed, and this withdraws that half and nothing else. The operator who set that condition is the one withdrawing it, and the loopback-only listener, the resident-minted credentials and the rest of the supported-host posture are untouched. I will say this explicitly in the review request so the reviewer does not request changes on the ground that it contradicts 00279a9c.\n\nBranch request/serve-drop-acknowledge-flag from current main, Rests-On naming this request, artifacts at cmd/gs, docs and README.md, full gate at the exact head, independent review before merge."}